<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Phase 4 Best in Slot Gear list for Unholy Death Knight DPS in Wrath of the Lich King Classic. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from Icecrown Citadel. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">
<span class="c6">Best in Slot Gear for Unholy Death Knight DPS Phase 4</span></h2>ICC continues the trend of (mostly) standardized item level for raid difficulties, meaning we're no longer forced to pick between tier and higher item level gear from hardmodes, and allows for the usage of tier bonuses without an Ilevel loss.<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Strength - is still the absolute best stat for Unholy Death Knights, this will not change throughout the expansion.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Hit - to at least 8% Melee Hit  so your ghoul, gargoyle, and army of the dead as well as main hand specials will be capped, any point of hit after this will increase your spell hit and white auto attack hit chance. <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=50138/nerves-of-cold-steel">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_dualwield.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nerves of Cold Steel</span></a> does not affect your summon or spell hit, but does work for your own melee attacks and specials (when dual wielding, as we will discuss below.)</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Haste - because we value increasing our gargoyles attack speed so much, on top of the base attack speed gain of haste, this stat is incredibly attractive to us.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Crit - is a great stat because of how it empowers our AoE as not only can our blood plague crit with our previous tier (which we will continue to use for any cleave/<wbr/>trash, as well as for a good duration into the tier,) <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=49655/wandering-plague">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_callofbone.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Wandering Plague</span></a> is also based off of our crit rating.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Expertise - Expertise has less of a gain for Death Knight's compared to most classes, as our special abilities don't charge us runes if they're dodged, but that strike will still be delayed the lost GCD, and your white hits can be dodged.</div></li></ol>
<div style="text-align: -webkit-center;"></div>
<br/>
<br/>With the change in how Hardmode gear works in the previous tier, the focus on Ilevel over stat preferences is largely done away with, instead allowing us to wear off pieces and tier that give us the best possible stats without losing out on additional strength. With that, our four set is fairly lackluster compared to other classes, especially weighed against the still staggering power of our ToC tier's four set bonus. Because of this, I highly recommend prio'ing tier as your smallest increase in general. <br/>
<br/>This phase finally sees the rise of 2h Unholy to the forefront, though this comes with the large caveat that this is only true with <a class="q5 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49623/shadowmourne">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_axe_113.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shadowmourne</span></a>. Thankfully there's very little change in gearing besides this, and you can comfortably transition from DW to 2H as soon as your guild rewards you with that coveted legendary. <br/>
<br/>That being said, this set includes <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50363/deathbringers-will">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_04.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Deathbringer's Will</span></a>, which comes with a very large caveat that should be read in the trinkets field below in this guide, as while it is BiS for Unholy, it is much less important for us, than it is other specs and classes. <br/>
