<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="emblems">
<span class="c6">Emblems of Triumph for Unholy Death Knight DPS Phase 4</span></h3>Tier is the obvious winner for most spots, both the heroic version, as well as the normal 25 version. I'd strongly recommend using your badges and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=52025/vanquishers-mark-of-sanctification">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_shieldofthetemplar.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vanquisher's Mark of Sanctification</span></a> on getting four set as fast as possible after buying your sigil. The trinket from badges is also a totally fine optional item, though it performs worse than previous tiers trinkets, and with the introduction of a farmable <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45609/comets-trail">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_arcane_starfire.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Comet's Trail</span></a> through Heroic+++ it's certainly less viable and markedly more work. <br/>
<br/>The sigil is the largest dps increase for badges for any single item (once you have SM,) but is less dps than completing your 4set and is also a dps loss until you're using a 2H. My recommendation is to buy your tier first, just to get it started, as you likely won't be using any of these items as you get them. <br/>
<br/>With that, the tier bonuses for Unholy aren't exceptionally strong for DW, and so it's easier to just wear full off pieces, and none of the tier, until you get your legendary. Tier 4set is still better than full off pieces, but we gain so little compared to other classes from our tier bonuses, that I highly recommend you just scoop the free 277 off pieces, and/<wbr/>or wear your T9 4p until others pick up their T10. <br/>
<br/>
